    "body": "@maximbaz Thinking it over, all that would be needed for an async prompt would be having the ability to print sections individually, right?\r\n\r\nI'm thinking that the API could perhaps be the following:\r\n```bash\r\nstarship --order   # print segment names in prompt order\r\nstarship [segment] # print a segment by its name\r\nstarship           # print the whole prompt synchronously\r\n```\r\nWith this API, instead of status being passed in as an argument, it would be given as an environment variable.\r\n\r\nGiven that API, would it be possible to create the worker jobs necessary to create async prompt with starship?\r\n\r\nI figure it'd be faster to ask y'all than it would be to learn the ins-and-outs of zsh-async. 😄 ",
